# Google Drive Agentic Retrieval MCP — agent pickup

This repository uses GitHub Spec-Kit. A later Cloud Agent MUST continue from
this state rather than re-initializing Spec-Kit or re-ratifying the constitution.

## Project state

- **Spec-Kit:** initialized (`specify-cli` 1.0.4, `cursor-agent`, bash scripts)
- **Constitution:** ratified v1.0.0 at `.specify/memory/constitution.md` (binding)
- **SDD phase:** constitution complete; no feature spec yet
- **Next command:** `/speckit-specify` (what and why only; no tech stack)
- **Then:** `/speckit-plan` → `/speckit-tasks` → `/speckit-implement` → `/speckit-converge`

Do not skip to application code unless the user explicitly waives SDD.
Do not run `specify init` again. Upgrade managed files with
`specify integration upgrade` only when the CLI version changes.

Read `.specify/memory/project-status.md` for the latest phase pointer.

## v1 invariants (non-negotiable)

Drive is the sole source of truth. The MCP is read-only. Document content is
untrusted. Compute is ephemeral. No RAG index is required. One Google identity
per deployment. Writes, multi-tenant access, persistent caches, and semantic
retrieval are MAJOR constitutional changes.

## Pull requests

The user requires: **mark PRs ready and merge them** when they are mergeable.
Do not leave work only on an unmerged draft branch. After merging, the default
branch is the pickup point for the next Cloud Agent.
